.TH WMFILES 1 "wm-desktop" "wm-desktop" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wmfiles \- column file browser that follows the Window Maker theme
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wmfiles
[\fIdirectory\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shows folders as columns (three visible). Click a folder to open it in the next column; double-click a file to open it
with $WMFILES_OPENER (default xdg\-open). The columns follow the disk, so changes made elsewhere appear on their own.
Colours, gradients and fonts come from the active Window Maker theme and are re-read when it changes.
File operations never overwrite, never follow symbolic links, and are all undoable.
.SH KEYS
.TP
Up, Down, Left, Right
Move; Right enters the next column.
.TP
Return
Open a file or enter a folder.
.TP
Space, Ctrl+A, Esc
Mark the item and move down; mark everything in the column; clear marks. Ctrl+click toggles, Shift+click marks a range.
.TP
Delete
Move the marked items (or the current one) to the XDG trash.
.TP
n, F2
New folder; rename. A name is typed in the bar at the bottom: Return accepts, Escape cancels.
.TP
Ctrl+C, Ctrl+X, Ctrl+V
Copy, cut, paste into the active column's folder.
.TP
o
Open with a command typed in the bar; the files are appended as arguments.
.TP
Ctrl+Z
Undo the last operation (32 steps; one step covers all items of one operation).
.TP
t, r
Switch to the trash and back; in the trash, restore the selected item to where it came from.
.TP
h
Show or hide hidden files.
.TP
q
Quit.
.SH MOUSE
Right-click for a menu (Open, Open with, Rename, New folder, Copy, Cut, Paste, Move to Trash). Drag rows onto a
folder or another column to move them; hold Ctrl while dropping to copy. The wheel scrolls.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WMFILES_OPENER
Command used to open files (default xdg\-open).
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Location of the trash (default ~/.local/share/Trash).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wmnotify (1),
.BR wmsettings (1)
